sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant B as Customer Browser
  participant CC as CheckoutController
  participant CS as CheckoutService
  participant DB as SQL Server
  participant ST as Stripe API
  B->>CC: POST /Checkout/Pay (shipping + AntiForgery token)
  CC->>CS: CreateOrderAndSessionAsync(userId, shipping)
  CS->>DB: Load cart + products (current price and stock)
  CS->>DB: BEGIN TX: insert Order PendingPayment, OrderItems, reserve stock, insert Payment Pending
  DB-->>CS: COMMIT ok
  CS->>ST: Create Checkout Session (line items, metadata OrderId, expires_at)
  ST-->>CS: Session Id + Url
  CS->>DB: Save StripeCheckoutSessionId on Payment
  CS-->>CC: Session Url
  CC-->>B: 303 Redirect to Stripe Url
  B->>ST: Customer pays with test card
  ST-->>B: Redirect to /Checkout/Success?orderId=...
  B->>CC: GET /Checkout/Success
  CC->>DB: Read Order status
  CC-->>B: Page: payment is being confirmed
  Note over ST,DB: The redirect NEVER marks the order as paid. Only the signed webhook does (Diagram 17)
